     "accumulator_evidence": "inherited from eyeriss_like",
     "citation": "Same JSSC 52(1), 2017 as eyeriss_like.  Differs from it in ONE block: the 8 kB filter allocation the paper describes -- \"the remaining 8 kB (two banks of 512-b x 64-b SRAMs) of the GLB is allocated for filter weights to compensate for insufficient off-chip traffic bandwidth\" -- is declared as a Timeloop storage level instead of !Nothing. Unlike eyeriss_v2_like_wglb, whose weight level is NOT in its paper, this level IS published; what is uncertain is whether a prefetch buffer should be modelled as a reuse level.  The pair BRACKETS that uncertainty: eyeriss_like is the upper bound on DRAM weight traffic (and so on the ECC saving), eyeriss_like_wglb the lower bound. Quote the pair, never one alone.",
